<title>USA: Exxon sees further downstream difficulties.</title>
<headline>Exxon sees further downstream difficulties.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp chief executive Lee Raymond said he expects downstream operations to continue to be difficult.</p>
<p>&quot;We remain skeptical about a turn around in this industry,&quot; Raymond told the Howard Weil Energy Conference Monday.</p>
<p>He said Exxon will continue to look at joint ventures and would sell any refinery which could not be turned around. But he declined to comment on which refinery might fit this category. ((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
